"""Shared party/quantity instructions required for all invoice AI providers."""
RULES=(
    'Follow this sales-invoice procedure in order. '
    '1. Confirm document_type as sales_invoice, credit_note, debit_note, purchase_order, quotation, delivery_note or unknown. '
    'A supplier-issued tax invoice is a sales invoice; do not turn an order, quotation or credit note into a Sales voucher. '
    '2. Read the exact printed invoice number and invoice date first. Invoice date has priority over due date, order date, dispatch date or shipping date. '
    'Never substitute today, a filename or a sequential number. Return null when unreadable. '
    '3. Identify seller from Supplier, Seller, From, Issued By or the invoice masthead; read seller_name, seller_gstin, seller_address and seller_state together. '
    '4. Identify buyer from Bill To, Buyer, Customer, Sold To, Invoiced To, Billed To, Supplied To, Consignee, Recipient or a To panel using its role and context, not a fixed keyword alone. '
    'Prefer the billed/legal buyer when billing and shipping differ. A Ship To or Delivered To panel may establish buyer only when the document unambiguously identifies that recipient as the purchasing party and has no conflicting billing party. '
    'Never substitute a transporter, bank, salesperson or signatory for buyer or seller. '
    'Keep each name, address and GSTIN in its own party role; if ambiguous return null, never copy the seller into buyer. '
    '5. Prioritize buyer_name, buyer_address, buyer_state and place_of_supply, then buyer_gstin and registration. '
    'Buyer state and place of supply are separate facts and can differ. Do not copy shipping state into buyer state or infer POS merely from a GSTIN. '
    '6. Read reverse_charge as Yes, No or null from an explicit RCM/reverse-charge declaration. Reverse Charge: No means No; zero tax alone does not establish RCM. '
    'For confirmed RCM sales, supplier-payable CGST/SGST/IGST/cess are zero; keep any printed nonzero tax amounts for conflict review, never erase them. '
    'Keep printed statutory item GST rates even when tax is payable by the recipient; do not label RCM exempt or nil-rated. '
    '7. Read every sold stock/service row into items: exact name, HSN/SAC, quantity, selling unit, unit price, taxable value, separate cgst_rate, sgst_rate, igst_rate and printed_total when shown. '
    'Do not treat tax-summary rows, carried-forward totals or repeated page headings as stock. Never invent a missing HSN or rate. '
    '8. Read taxable total, separate cgst/sgst/igst/cess amounts, round_off and grand total; preserve the printed bifurcation, not just aggregate GST. '
    '9. Use only compatible imported company masters when offered. For unmatched items retain invoice product/HSN/tax facts for a new master; a similar name alone is insufficient evidence. '
    '10. All extracted values are editable review drafts. Missing or conflicting facts require source review before Tally import. '
    'Printed selling units and explicit quantity suffixes outrank assumptions. If missing, use product/packaging reasoning for PCS, Units, BOX, LTR, KG or other appropriate units. '
    'Return unit_basis printed/inferred and unit_reason. Qty is a heading, not a selling unit. '
    'Never scale numeric quantity, rate or value, or mistake medicine strength for sold weight/volume. '
    'Identify the currency of returned accounting amounts from printed codes, names or symbols. '
    'Return an ISO code only when unambiguous; $ alone is ambiguous, retain it for review. '
    'For foreign-only amounts return the printed monetary values unchanged in their source currency; Python converts to INR. '
    'Read exchange_rate only if printed: exchange_rate_basis is INR_per_foreign for INR per one foreign unit, '
    'or foreign_per_INR for foreign units per INR. exchange_rate_units is the printed denominator unit count '
    '(normally 1; for INR 55 per 100 JPY return rate 55, units 100, basis INR_per_foreign). '
    'Never invent a missing exchange rate or use a current market rate; set exchange_rate_basis to unknown if direction is unclear. '
    'When INR accounting totals and item prices are printed, currency is INR; keep those INR values '
    'and report foreign_currency and exchange_rate separately. Never mix foreign item amounts with INR totals. '
)
